      "body": "## Purpose\n\nEngine start fails with prefill context parallel, MTP and prefill CUDA graphs together, for example:\n- `--prefill-context-parallel-size 8 --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",...}'`\n- `--compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\":\"PIECEWISE\",...}'`\n\nThe failure is in `capture()` of the speculator (`spec_decode/target_dependent_ar/speculator.py`), while it captures the draft model's prefill graphs:\n- The capture runs `_prefill` on generic dummy inputs.\n- Under PCP, the draft prefill instead reads the inputs that the PCP manager prepares (`prepare_draft_prefill` / `draft_prefill_batch`).\n- For DSA models the sparse indexer then fails during capture:\n\n```\nFile \".../vllm/model_executor/layers/sparse_attn_indexer.py\", line 723, in sparse_attn_indexer\nFile \".../vllm/utils/deep_gemm.py\", line 635, in mqa_logits_mx_inputs\ntorch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: invalid argument\n```\n\nThe fix skips the draft prefill capture when a PCP manager is present. Dispatch then finds no prefill graph for the draft and runs it eagerly, while the target model keeps its prefill graphs. Without PCP nothing changes.\n\n## Test Plan\n\nGLM-5.3 FP8 and NVFP4 on 8×B300 (SM103):\n- `--prefill-context-parallel-size 8 --enable-expert-parallel`;\n- MTP with 1 speculative token;\n- `cudagraph_mode: PIECEWISE`, capture sizes 256–4096.\n\n## Test Result\n\n- **Before:** engine core initialization fails with the traceback above.\n- **After:** the engine starts and serves. The log shows `PCP: draft prefill runs eagerly (no prefill CUDA graphs).`\n- **Latency:** cold 2k / 4k / 16k / 64k prefills take 77 / 70 / 181 / 708 ms (NVFP4 checkpoint, DeepGEMM MegaMoE experts).\n- **Accuracy:** I ran the same change on a v0.31.0 build with the FP8 checkpoint. GSM8K was 96.51% vs 96.59% without prefill graphs (McNemar p = 1.0), and a needle-in-a-haystack check passed 20/20.\n\n`pre-commit` passes.\n",
